          "docs": "Temporarily suspends future executions of a scheduled deployment action without deleting the schedule configuration. The schedule remains configured and can be reactivated at any time using the ResumeScheduledDeployment endpoint. This is useful for temporarily halting recurring schedules (drift detection, TTL, or custom) during maintenance periods or when troubleshooting issues."
