          "docs": "Creates a TTL (time-to-live) schedule for a stack using Pulumi Deployments. TTL schedules automatically destroy a stack's cloud resources at a specified expiration time, which is useful for temporary or ephemeral infrastructure that should be cleaned up after a defined period. The 'timestamp' field must be an ISO 8601 formatted date-time (e.g. '2024-12-31T00:00:00.000Z') specifying when the destroy operation should execute. When 'deleteAfterDestroy' is set to true, the stack itself is also remov"
